From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Junod <donujp@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:43:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(session): add SessionOptions::disable_auto_restore

When persistence is configured, Session::new_with_opts reads every stored
torrent and adds it back while the session is being constructed. An
application that keeps its own queue (and wants to decide which torrents
come back, in what order, and with which options) has no way to opt out
of this while still using persistence and fast-resume: the only choices
are to restore everything or to turn persistence off.

Add SessionOptions::disable_auto_restore (default false). When true,
persistence and fast-resume stay enabled but the constructor does not
add the stored torrents. The caller re-adds the ones it wants with
add_torrent, and AddTorrentOptions::preferred_id lets it keep the stored
torrent id, so the persisted record (and its fast-resume state) is
picked up again.

The default is unchanged.

The test creates two persisted torrents, then opens the same persistence
folder three times: with auto-restore disabled (no torrents are
admitted), re-adding one torrent by preferred_id (it resumes from the
stored piece state rather than re-checking the files), and with the
default (both torrents come back).
